      "sourceEvidenceMode": "live-public-fetch",
      "sourceCount": 2,
      "answer": "The client keeps HTTPX’s environment proxy mounts and `NO_PROXY` behavior by leaving the default transport in place and setting `trust_env=True` when no custom transport is supplied; `verify=True` retains certificate verification. A request hook restricts HTTPS destinations to `opencode.ai` on the permitted port and requires an allowed method/path, while rejecting credentials, queries, and fragments. Redirects are disabled, and the default transport has zero retries. [S1]\n\n**Tested:** a proxy connection failure raises without retry or direct fallback. [S2] The supplied test does not itself verify CA behavior or the destination and redirect restrictions.\n\nSHA-256: `a9642da7ebb756f1b0e0c15578b576e30f75fd542ab6fbb0d4702a3da18dcde4`",
